{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"dramatic-sombrous-chickadee","creation_channel":"python","description":"# Gate blindness to world-grounded evidence: force measurement provenance into the record\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nA `/rebar-implement` run of epic `061c-ecd1-8967-4a76` landed five changes through every gate. **The gates\nperformed to their design envelope.** Plan-review blocked infeasible mechanics (a tenacity-transport claim that\ncannot wrap boto3; an `isinstance` against a botocore-dependent class; a live canary path that would have made\nbillable AWS calls on every CI run). The completion-verifier twice refused a close whose stated criteria had no\ntest. Full-suite pre-flight caught cross-module regressions `tests/unit` missed.\n\nEvery one of those catches shares a property: **the ground truth lived in the repo**, where the reviewer's\nread/grep tools could reach it.\n\nFour escapes got through, and they are one defect wearing different clothes — **a green signal whose\nmeasurement could not have observed the failure it claims to rule out**:\n\n1. **Wrong environment.** Bedrock caching and model-availability measurements were taken in account\n   `579718921998` / `us-east-2` and recorded as settled fact; the project runs in `896586841071` / `us-east-1`\n   (named by the Terraform backend `rebar-tfstate-896586841071`). No gate compares a claim's observation\n   context against the project's environment. A human caught it by asking \"is that this project's account?\"\n2. **Instruments that cannot observe the failure — twice, in the same investigation.** This escape is the\n   epic's sharpest example precisely because the *first correction was also wrong*.\n\n   **2a.** Live `bedrock:Converse` calls validated a *scoped* IAM grant while running under an identity\n   holding `bedrock:*`. Evidence generated under broader privilege than production is structurally unable to\n   fail, so its success carries **zero information**.\n\n   **2b.** The prescribed remedy — `aws iam simulate-principal-policy` against the role — then produced a\n   confident, recorded, and **wrong** conclusion: that `bedrock:Converse` was the action to grant. The\n   simulator answered exactly the question asked (\"would this policy permit the action *named*\n   `bedrock:Converse`?\", legitimately no, since that action genuinely exists) but **not** the question that\n   mattered (\"which action does the Converse API actually *check*?\"). Only a real call FROM the instance\n   revealed the truth — `AccessDeniedException ... not authorized to perform: bedrock:InvokeModel` — meaning\n   the ORIGINAL plan was right and the \"fix\" broke it, on a role feeding `eb6e-f43a-e86b-443a`, a cutover\n   with no fallback.\n\n   The pair is the lesson: a wildcard identity could not fail, and a simulator could not fail *for the reason\n   that mattered*. **Evidence is only as good as its ability to have come out the other way for the reason\n   you care about** — and swapping one instrument for a more rigorous-sounding one does not establish that.\n3. **Tests that cannot fail** — the code-side form of the same defect: a contrast case whose discriminating\n   conjunct was never exercised, and an oracle asserting on an object where production passes a string.\n   **Both WERE caught** (mutation testing; the LLM reviewer) precisely because they are repo-checkable. That\n   contrast is the evidence for this epic's thesis.\n4. **Confidence outrunning method**: \"verified by reading\" was a hand-picked grep that missed a dependency;\n   \"18/18 green\" was reported while typecheck was red.\n\n## Why 1 and 2 are structural, not a calibration miss\n\n`verified_at_sha` pins the code world completely and the outside world not at all. Plan-review runs **before**\nthe evidence exists, so it cannot audit a measurement not yet taken; the completion-verifier accepts\n`[operator-attested]` evidence **on trust by design** (ADR-0043). One gate cannot audit it, the other is\ndesigned not to. The in-flight T5c rewrite pushes grounding toward current code and IaC state but still cannot\nobserve a live cloud account — nothing in the current design can, and nothing should try.\n\n## Approach\n\nDo **not** make a gate observe the world. Force the measurement's context into the record as text, then let the\nexisting repo-grounded machinery find contradictions in it. Detail lives in the child story; the shape is:\n\n1. Extend the attested-evidence contract with measurement-provenance fields — environment, principal, and\n   privilege posture relative to production.\n2. Enforce their **presence** deterministically, zero LLM, mirroring\n   `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_operator_attested.py` (DET-first doctrine).\n3. Let an LLM criterion judge the *declaration* against repo facts — once provenance is text, \"plan attests\n   account X, IaC names account Y\" becomes a **repo-checkable contradiction**, which is exactly what the\n   gate's strongest criteria already do well.\n4. Land the generalized rule as an **advisory** criterion per ADR-0054; corpus replay decides promotion.\n\n## Explicitly rejected\n\n- **Making the completion-verifier re-run world measurements.** Expensive, flaky, recursive — the verifier's\n  own credentials carry the same privilege-masking problem, so it would validate using the instrument under\n  suspicion.\n- **Escape 4 as gate scope.** Reported-green-while-red is *reporting discipline*, already covered by the\n  orchestration rule that agents report gate output faithfully rather than narrating success. Filing it as a\n  gate gap would be mis-attribution.\n- **Wording changes alone.** The contract was followed and still failed; emphasis is not the defect. This is\n  the same lesson as epic `9109-2ad9-2477-4cf6` (Serena tool-choice), which is why that epic's structural\n  framing is the model here rather than its subject matter.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] an `[operator-attested]` criterion lacking measurement provenance is flagged by a DETERMINISTIC check\n      (no LLM) — `det_measurement_provenance.py`, surfaced advisory through `p6_ac_quality`, landed in\n      change 1423 with a mutation-tested oracle (breaking the binding rule, placeholder detection or enum\n      membership each kills tests)\n- [x] the new criterion ships **advisory** (ADR-0054) and rides the `.rebar/` project overlay, leaving the\n      shipped default criteria set unchanged for other rebar clients\n- [x] an ADR records the amended evidence contract, citing ADR-0043 as the shape it changes\n- [x] the completion-verifier is NOT made to re-run world measurements — the rejected alternative stays\n      rejected, and a test or grep demonstrates it\n\n## Descoped to `98df-3528-9b1f-405a` (ridiculous-expert-mouse), filed as an `idea`\n\nAC-1 originally also required the wrong-account escape to be **reproduced as a regression fixture** from the\nreal `579718921998` vs `896586841071` case. That clause is NOT delivered and is NOT claimed as done.\n\nReproducing it means exercising the AGENT criterion's rule (a) semantically, which needs an eval corpus\n(`.rebar/evals/plan-review-project-measurement-provenance.eval.yaml`) plus a live run — the same behavioural\nhalf descoped from story `f161`. Both moved to `98df`, which also carries the rule (b)/(c)/(d) fixtures and\nthe ADR-0054 corpus-replay false-positive rate that would justify promoting the criterion from advisory.\n\nThis epic therefore closes on its MECHANISM being delivered and proven — provenance is now forced into the\nrecord as text, deterministically enforced, and judged by a tool-enabled criterion — not on that criterion's\nfiring behaviour having been calibrated. The distinction is safe because the criterion ships **advisory**: it\ncannot block any claim or close, so an uncalibrated advisory criterion is inert-but-useful rather than risky.\nPromotion is a separate ADR-0054 decision nobody has committed to, which is why `98df` is an `idea`.","id":"1d24-b12c-c2c1-4ffe","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Gate blindness to world-grounded evidence: force measurement provenance into the record"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788223344602914001,"uuid":"25c90bc3-8abd-4487-b8d9-03676d981c8a"}